From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] query_dma: EDEN_NX2_QUERY_FLIP_TRACE and EDEN_NX2_RENDER_ALWAYS, to name what
 switches the white shapes on and off

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series), off unless one of the two switches is set.
Debug only. Not a fix.

In run183 a rock by the camera turns white in blocks of mostly 2 game frames on, 2 off, for 8 s with
the camera still. Nothing in the logs moves with it. Occlusion reports are the first suspect: macro
0x142 reads reports (word 0 is the sample count, often 0, seen in the Linux run's log), and Lichii
PR 215 (WeslieDE) ties white flashes to stale reads of them (976 in 2.5 minutes in its trace, all
macro 0xe2c, method 0x158). But nobody has seen one of our reports flip in time with a flash:
EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_TRACE gives words for its first 4000 reads only, and logs nothing at all unless
the read covers a report it counts as pending. run185 had it on and logged nothing.

EDEN_NX2_QUERY_FLIP_TRACE=1: Maxwell3D::FrontDmaRead notes the first 4 words of every FIFOed macro
read (method 0x158), each word on its own, in a table of 16384 slots. Once a second it logs up to 16
words that went between zero and non-zero at least 3 times, with their last 32 reads as bits, so a
report in step with the flash reads ...1100110011... dev= is the address EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_CUT_LOG logs
for the same report. A flip here with none there means the game read something other than what was
written last: a late report. The 3D engine also logs once a second how many draws ran and were
skipped by render enable, how often render_enable.mode was written and with which mode, and what
render_enable_override held at the draws. That register is only looked at inside
ProcessQueryCondition, so a macro that writes it alone changes nothing here: "override at draws"
shows whether that happens. Draws are counted in ProcessDraw, so indirect draws aren't in these
numbers. A count of 0 mode writes says render enable isn't used at all.

The host compare is not traced. On this port hcr_mode is 1 by default (headless/dev_vulkan.h), and
prepare-vulkan-port.py sends a condition with a report pending out of
HostConditionalRenderingCompareValues with false, into the CPU evaluation. Upstream's "return true"
at Low, where draws run whatever the report will say, does not ship here, so it isn't a suspect.
That block of vk_query_cache.cpp is also an anchor of prepare-vulkan-port.py: this patch must not
touch it, or adapt() skips the change, the build still passes, and the shipped code returns true.

EDEN_NX2_RENDER_ALWAYS=1: ProcessQueryCondition leaves execute_on true and never starts host
conditional rendering. If the flashes stop, a condition decides them. If the water's reflection
stays on too, the same condition hides it. If the macro skips draws by itself, it changes nothing,
and that proves nothing. It may draw things the game meant to hide, and cost fps.

Only the split's front path is traced (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2, the default for these titles). The macro.cpp
read path for lower split modes isn't. Unset, nothing changes. Not built, not run.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/query_dma.h b/src/video_core/query_dma.h
--- a/src/video_core/query_dma.h
+++ b/src/video_core/query_dma.h
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
 #include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
 #include <cstdlib>
 
 #include <fmt/ranges.h>
@@ -45,6 +46,138 @@
     return mode;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_QUERY_FLIP_TRACE=1: logs which occlusion reports change between zero and non-zero
+/// read after read, and what the 3D engine's render enable does. QUERY_DMA_TRACE stops giving
+/// words after 4000 reads, a second or two at Ocarina's rate, so it can't see a late flash.
+inline bool FlipTraceEnabled() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_QUERY_FLIP_TRACE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
+/// EDEN_NX2_RENDER_ALWAYS=1: render enable conditions are ignored and every draw runs, on the host
+/// too. Asks whether a condition decides the flashes. It can show objects meant to be hidden.
+inline bool RenderAlways() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_RENDER_ALWAYS");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
+struct FlipSlot {
+    GPUVAddr source;
+    DAddr device;  ///< The same word as ZPASS_CUT_LOG names it, 0 if unmapped
+    u64 bits;      ///< One bit a read, newest lowest: 1 when the word wasn't zero
+    u32 last_word;
+    u32 macro;
+    u32 reads;     ///< This second
+    u32 flips;     ///< This second
+};
+
+/// Notes one word of a report read. The split's front only. Once a second, logs the words that
+/// flipped at least 3 times, 16 at most, with their last 32 reads as bits.
+inline void FlipTrace(u32 macro, GPUVAddr source, DAddr device, u32 word) {
+    static constexpr size_t table_size = size_t{1} << 14;
+    static constexpr size_t max_probes = 8;
+    static constexpr u32 min_flips = 3;
+    static constexpr size_t max_lines = 16;
+    static std::array<FlipSlot, table_size> table{};
+    static u64 total_reads{};
+    static u64 untracked{};
+    static auto next_report = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds{1};
+
+    ++total_reads;
+    FlipSlot* slot = nullptr;
+    const size_t index = static_cast<size_t>(((source >> 2) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL) >> 50);
+    for (size_t probe = 0; probe < max_probes; ++probe) {
+        FlipSlot& candidate = table[(index + probe) & (table_size - 1)];
+        if (candidate.source == source || candidate.source == 0) {
+            slot = &candidate;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (slot == nullptr) {
+        ++untracked;
+    } else {
+        const bool non_zero = word != 0;
+        if (slot->source != 0 && non_zero != ((slot->bits & 1) != 0)) {
+            ++slot->flips;
+        }
+        slot->source = source;
+        slot->device = device;
+        slot->macro = macro;
+        slot->bits = (slot->bits << 1) | (non_zero ? 1 : 0);
+        slot->last_word = word;
+        ++slot->reads;
+    }
+    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+    if (now < next_report) {
+        return;
+    }
+    next_report = now + std::chrono::seconds{1};
+    size_t lines = 0;
+    u64 flipping = 0;
+    for (FlipSlot& entry : table) {
+        if (entry.flips >= min_flips) {
+            ++flipping;
+            if (lines < max_lines) {
+                ++lines;
+                LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                         "Query flip: gpu={:#x} dev={:#x} macro={:#x} reads={} flips={} "
+                         "bits={:032b} last={:#x}",
+                         entry.source, entry.device, entry.macro, entry.reads, entry.flips,
+                         entry.bits & 0xffffffffULL, entry.last_word);
+            }
+        }
+        entry.reads = 0;
+        entry.flips = 0;
+    }
+    if (flipping != 0) {
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Query flip: {} reports flipped this second, {} reads, {} untracked",
+                 flipping, total_reads, untracked);
+    }
+}
+
+struct RenderEnableCounts {
+    std::array<u64, 8> mode_writes{}; ///< By regs.render_enable.mode
+    std::array<u64, 4> overrides{};   ///< By regs.render_enable_override at each draw
+    u64 draws{};
+    u64 skipped{};
+};
+
+inline RenderEnableCounts& RenderEnableStats() {
+    static RenderEnableCounts counts;
+    return counts;
+}
+
+/// A write to render_enable.mode. The thread that runs the engine's methods only.
+inline void NoteCondition(u32 mode) {
+    ++RenderEnableStats().mode_writes[mode & 7];
+}
+
+/// A draw from ProcessDraw, run or skipped: indirect draws don't come here. The thread that runs
+/// the engine's methods only. Logs once a second.
+inline void NoteDraw(bool executed, u32 override_value) {
+    RenderEnableCounts& counts = RenderEnableStats();
+    ++counts.draws;
+    ++counts.overrides[override_value & 3];
+    counts.skipped += executed ? 0 : 1;
+    static auto next_report = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds{1};
+    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+    if (now < next_report) {
+        return;
+    }
+    next_report = now + std::chrono::seconds{1};
+    LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+             "Render enable: {} draws, {} skipped, mode writes {}, override at draws {}",
+             counts.draws, counts.skipped, fmt::join(counts.mode_writes, ","),
+             fmt::join(counts.overrides, ","));
+    counts = RenderEnableCounts{};
+}
+
 /// Whether [source, source + size) holds reports still waiting for host query results. Runs
 /// where the rasterizer's caches are owned (the back of a split GPU thread). A report that has
 /// landed counts too until it is unregistered: nothing sets IsGuestSynced here.
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
@@ -686,6 +686,13 @@
 }
 
 void Maxwell3D::ProcessQueryCondition() {
+    if (VideoCommon::QueryDma::FlipTraceEnabled()) [[unlikely]] {
+        VideoCommon::QueryDma::NoteCondition(static_cast<u32>(regs.render_enable.mode));
+    }
+    if (VideoCommon::QueryDma::RenderAlways()) [[unlikely]] {
+        execute_on = true;
+        return;
+    }
     if (rasterizer->AccelerateConditionalRendering()) {
         execute_on = true;
         return;
@@ -1233,6 +1240,15 @@
             fs.parameters.push_back(word);
         } else if (ram + i < native_data_ram.size()) {
             native_data_ram[ram + i] = word;
+        }
+    }
+    if (VideoCommon::QueryDma::FlipTraceEnabled() && method == 0x158) [[unlikely]] {
+        // Each word on its own: NX2_NOTES says this macro reads two counters.
+        for (u32 i = 0; i < std::min<u32>(words, 4); ++i) {
+            const GPUVAddr word_address = source + u64{i} * sizeof(u32);
+            VideoCommon::QueryDma::FlipTrace(macro, word_address,
+                                             memory_manager.GpuToCpuAddress(word_address).value_or(0),
+                                             memory_manager.Read<u32>(word_address));
         }
     }
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "common/settings.h"
 #include "video_core/dirty_flags.h"
 #include "video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.h"
+#include "video_core/query_dma.h"
 #include "video_core/rasterizer_interface.h"
 #include "video_core/macro.h"
 
@@ -318,6 +319,10 @@
         draw_indexed ? draw_state.index_buffer.count : draw_state.vertex_buffer.count;
     LOG_TRACE(HW_GPU, "called, topology={}, count={}", draw_state.topology, draw_indexed ? draw_state.index_buffer.count : draw_state.vertex_buffer.count);
     UpdateTopology(maxwell3d);
+    if (VideoCommon::QueryDma::FlipTraceEnabled()) [[unlikely]] {
+        VideoCommon::QueryDma::NoteDraw(maxwell3d.ShouldExecute(),
+                                        static_cast<u32>(maxwell3d.regs.render_enable_override));
+    }
     if (maxwell3d.ShouldExecute()) {
         if (draw_indexed && maxwell3d.regs.IsShaderConfigEnabled(4)) {
             maxwell3d.GetNativeMacroEngine().RecordBananzaTerrainDepthDraw(maxwell3d, instance_count);
